SOAPBOX: Actually, my plan was to beat national record in Classic LP (which was not too high - 650k), and at the end I was 200k over European Classic LP record.
SOAPBOX: LY5W did fantastic job and claimed World record in classic LP. Hat off Sam, preety sure, after surgery wasn't easy to find enough energy for contesting.
SOAPBOX: As 100W station and "attractive" DX land it wasn't easy to make any run. Over 700 Qs were S/P. It means a looooot of work with VFO knob. I must admit, Maestro did fantastic job, it was so easy work with it.
SOAPBOX: Another thing is unassisted category. All logged juicy multipliers are mix of luck, VFO dialing and condx knowledge. Not too many multis on CQ (FM4, VP9, CO)
SOAPBOX: The most surprized QSO was KL7SB (1st call!) on 40m with huuuuge signal, decoded over 2h long here in EU.
SOAPBOX: With rearanged break times, I guess 1.6+M was possible from my QTH.
SOAPBOX: Flexradio 6600
SOAPBOX: 20-15-10m: LZA Beam (2 el per band) @10m high
SOAPBOX: 40m: L/4 ground plane
SOAPBOX: 40m: dipole
SOAPBOX: 80m: ground plane
SOAPBOX: 73, Zik DK8ZZ
